Non-magnetic (bronze) set issues (see link below):


In 1999, the Brilliant Uncirculated and Proof Annual sets featured pennies struck using bronze planchets, due to a world shortage of steel.


Reports have been received regarding differing number of beads to both sides:


1998-1999 115 beads on obverse and 113 beads on reverse;

2000-2008 110 beads on obverse and 109 beads on reverse;




© Heligal


Reports have also been received regarding reverse varieties for the 2000 & 2004 issues:


2000 1 points to left of dot;

2004 1 points to right of dot;





(former Spink ref. 4710)
